control substitution on

query
SHOW ALL;
----
name	setting	description
__iceberg_unsafe_struct_null_default_interp	NULL	DANGEROUS TESTING-ONLY SETTING: interpret a null Iceberg STRUCT default as an empty struct whose fields use their own defaults. The only non-null value accepted is '{}'.
access_mode	automatic	Access mode of the database (AUTOMATIC, READ_ONLY or READ_WRITE).
allocator_background_threads	off	Whether to enable the allocator background threads.
allocator_bulk_deallocation_flush_threshold	512.0 MiB	If a bulk deallocation larger than this occurs, flush outstanding allocations.
allocator_flush_threshold	134217728B	Peak allocation threshold at which to flush the allocator after completing a task.
allow_asterisks_in_http_paths	off	Allow '*' character in URLs users can query
allow_community_extensions	on	Allow loading extensions build by the community.
allow_extension_repositories	undecided	Whether custom trusted extension repositories are 'allowed', 'forbidden' (which also distrusts existing repositories) or 'undecided' (the default: blocks adding new repositories, but keeps trusting existing ones). While the database is running the setting can only move from 'undecided' to 'allowed' or 'forbidden', or from 'allowed' to 'forbidden'.
allow_extensions_metadata_mismatch	off	Allow to load extensions with no compatible metadata.
allow_persistent_secrets	on	Allow the creation of persistent secrets that are stored and loaded on restarts.
allow_unredacted_secrets	off	Allow printing unredacted secrets.
allow_unsigned_extensions	off	Allow to load extensions with invalid or missing signatures.
allowed_configs	[]	List of configuration options that are ALWAYS allowed to be changed, even when lock_configuration is true.
allowed_directories	[]	List of directories, and directory prefixes, that are ALWAYS allowed to be queried, even when enable_external_access is false.
allowed_paths	[]	List of files that are ALWAYS allowed to be queried, even when enable_external_access is false.
application_name	(empty)	Sets the application name to be reported in statistics and logs.
approximate_join_order_threshold	12	The minimum number of tables in a join to determine the optimal join order approximately instead of exactly.
arrow_large_buffer_size	off	Whether Arrow buffers for strings, blobs, UUIDs and bits should be exported using large buffers.
arrow_lossless_conversion	off	Whenever a DuckDB type does not have a clear native or canonical extension match in Arrow, export the types with a duckdb.type_name extension name.
arrow_output_list_view	off	Whether the export to the Arrow format should use ListView as the physical layout for LIST columns.
arrow_output_version	1.0	Whether strings should be produced by DuckDB in Utf8View format instead of Utf8.
asof_loop_join_threshold	64	The maximum number of rows we need on the left side of an ASOF join to use a nested loop join.
async_threads	<slt:ignore>	The number of total async threads used by the system for tasks like I/O.
auto_checkpoint_skip_wal_threshold	100000	The estimated WAL write size at which point we will skip writing to the WAL and only checkpoint. Skipping writing to the WAL means concurrent commits are blocked while the checkpoint is happening.
auto_fallback_to_full_download	on	Allows automatically falling back to full file downloads when possible.
autoinstall_extension_repository	(empty)	Overrides the custom endpoint for extension installation on autoloading. Falls back to custom_extension_repository, if not specified.
autoinstall_known_extensions	off	Whether known extensions are allowed to be automatically installed when a query depends on them.
autoload_known_extensions	off	Whether known extensions are allowed to be automatically loaded when a query depends on them.
azure_account_name	NULL	Azure account name, when set, the extension will attempt to automatically detect credentials
azure_context_caching	1	Enable/disable the caching of some context when performing queries. This cache is by default enable, and will for a given connection keep a local context when performing a query. If you suspect that the caching is causing some side effect you can try to disable it by setting this option to false.
azure_credential_chain	NULL	Ordered list of Azure credential providers, in string format separated by ';'. E.g. 'cli;workload_identity;managed_identity;env'
azure_endpoint	blob.core.windows.net	Override the azure endpoint for when the Azure credential providers are used.
azure_http_proxy	NULL	Proxy to use when login & performing request to azure. By default it will use the HTTP_PROXY environment variable if set.
azure_http_stats	0	Include http info from the Azure Storage in the explain analyze statement.
azure_proxy_password	NULL	Http proxy password if needed.
azure_proxy_user_name	NULL	Http proxy user name if needed.
azure_read_buffer_size	8388608	Size of the read buffer.
azure_storage_connection_string	NULL	Azure connection string, used for authenticating and configuring azure requests
azure_write_block_size	8388608	Size in bytes of each block for Blob/DFS writes. 0 restores the default (8 MiB). Max 4000 MiB (Azure per-request limit). Azure hard-limits a blob to 50,000 blocks; increase this to write files larger than 50,000 × azure_write_block_size bytes.
azure_write_staged_blocks_per_commit	0	Number of blocks staged before an intermediate CommitBlockList. 0 (default) disables intermediate commits; the full block list is committed on close. Non-zero values make partial writes visible sooner at the cost of extra commit RPCs. Does not affect the 50,000-block blob limit; increase azure_write_block_size for that.
binary_as_string	off	In Parquet files, interpret binary data as a string.
block_allocator_memory	0 bytes	Physical memory that the block allocator is allowed to use. This memory is allocated once, never freed, and cannot be reduced.
bytea_output	hex	Sets the output format for bytea.
ca_cert_file	(empty)	Path to a custom certificate file for self-signed certificates.
cache_local_files	off	Whether the external file cache also caches local files. Remote files are always cached.
Calendar	gregorian	The current calendar
catalog_error_max_schemas	100	The maximum number of schemas in the catalog that the system will scan to generate the "did you mean..." error message.
ch_binary_as_blob	off	Read ClickHouse String/FixedString columns as BLOB instead of VARCHAR
ch_connection_cache	on	Whether to reuse (pool) ClickHouse connections across statements; setting this to false bypasses the connection pool entirely (dynamic kill switch)
ch_debug_show_queries	off	DEBUG SETTING: print all queries sent to ClickHouse to stdout
ch_experimental_filter_pushdown	on	Whether or not to use filter pushdown
ch_order_pushdown	on	Push ORDER BY and LIMIT clauses to ClickHouse (default: true)
ch_pool_acquire_mode	force	How to acquire connections from the pool: 'force' (always connect, ignore pool limit), 'wait' (block until available), 'try' (fail immediately if unavailable) (default: force)
ch_pool_enable_reaper_thread	on	Whether to run the pool reaper thread that periodically closes connections exceeding 'ch_pool_max_lifetime_millis' or 'ch_pool_idle_timeout_millis'
ch_pool_enable_thread_local_cache	off	Whether to enable the connection caching in thread-local cache. Such connections are pinned to their threads and are not made available to other threads, while still taking a place in the pool
ch_pool_idle_timeout_millis	60000	Maximum number of milliseconds a connection can sit idle in the pool; checked on lease and, with the reaper thread enabled, in the background
ch_pool_max_connections	<slt:ignore>	Maximum number of connections that are allowed to be cached in a connection pool for each attached ClickHouse database
ch_pool_max_lifetime_millis	0	Maximum number of milliseconds a connection can be kept open; checked on lease/return and, with the reaper thread enabled, in the background
ch_pool_wait_timeout_millis	30000	Maximum number of milliseconds to wait when acquiring a connection from a pool where all available connections are already taken
ch_statement_timeout_millis	NULL	Maximum milliseconds a ClickHouse scan/execute query may run (0 = unlimited)
checkpoint_on_detach	DEFAULT	Override checkpoint behavior when detaching a database. ENABLED requests a checkpoint, but the checkpoint does not occur if another connection still references the database. DISABLED never checkpoints, DEFAULT defers to the global checkpoint_on_shutdown setting.
checkpoint_threshold	16.0 MiB	The WAL size threshold at which to automatically trigger a checkpoint, e.g. 1GB.
cleanup_interval_step	1	Number of commit ticks between background unreferenced-file cleanup passes for newly created inverted indexes and search tables. WITH (cleanup_interval_step = ...) overrides it per index or table. 0 disables cleanup. Default: 1.
client_encoding	UTF8	Sets the client's character set encoding.
client_min_messages	notice	Sets the message levels that are sent to the client.
compaction_floor_segment_bytes	2097152	Segments of an inverted index or search table below this size count as equal-sized for compaction candidate selection. WITH (compaction_floor_segment_bytes = ...) overrides it per index or table. Default 2097152 (2MB).
compaction_interval	1000	Background compaction interval (ms) for newly created inverted indexes and search tables. WITH (compaction_interval = ...) overrides it per index or table, ALTER INDEX / ALTER TABLE ... SET changes it later. 0 disables background compaction; VACUUM (COMPACT_*) still merges on demand. Default: 1000.
compaction_max_segments	10	Maximum segments of an inverted index or search table merged by one background compaction. WITH (compaction_max_segments = ...) overrides it per index or table. Default 10.
compaction_max_segments_bytes	5368709120	Byte budget of one background compaction of an inverted index or search table (the tier target size). WITH (compaction_max_segments_bytes = ...) overrides it per index or table. Default 5368709120 (5GB).
copy_csv_header_default	off	Whether COPY ... TO a CSV file writes a header line when HEADER is not specified
current_transaction_invalidation_policy	STANDARD_POLICY	Which types of exceptions invalidate the database for the current transaction.
custom_extension_repository	(empty)	Overrides the custom endpoint for extension installation.
custom_user_agent	(empty)	HTTP request metadata that can be set by callers/wrappers to tag their own traffic when DuckDB makes a request.
DateStyle	ISO, MDY	Sets the display format for date and time values.
debug_checkpoint_scan_sleep_ms	0	DEBUG SETTING: time to sleep after a checkpoint has written a table's row groups, before it installs them
default_block_size	262144	The default block size for new duckdb database files. New means that the file is being created and does not yet exist.
default_collation	(empty)	The collation setting used when none is specified.
default_null_order	NULLS_LAST	The NULL ordering used when none is specified (NULLS_FIRST or NULLS_LAST).
default_order	ASCENDING	The order type used when none is specified (ASC or DESC).
default_secret_storage	local_file	Allows switching the default storage for secrets.
default_transaction_invalidation_policy	ALL_ERRORS_INVALIDATE_TRANSACTION	When to invalidate transactions when errors occur. SYNTACTIC_ERRORS_DO_NOT_INVALIDATE means that parser and binder exceptions do not invalidate. ALL_ERRORS_INVALIDATE_TRANSACTION means all errors invalidate a transaction.
default_transaction_isolation	repeatable read	Sets the transaction isolation level of each new transaction.
default_transaction_read_only	off	Sets the default read-only status of new transactions.
delim_join_as_cte	on	Rewrite delim joins to materialized CTEs during dependent join flattening.
dialect_compatibility_mode	NONE	Enable SQL dialect compatibility for a certain engine, e.g. `SET dialect_compatibility_mode='spark'`.
disable_database_invalidation	on	Disables invalidating the database instance when encountering a fatal error. Should be used with great care, as DuckDB cannot guarantee correct behavior after a fatal error.
disable_parquet_prefetching	off	Disable the prefetching mechanism in Parquet
disable_timestamptz_casts	off	Disable casting from timestamp to timestamptz.
disabled_compression_methods	(empty)	Disable a specific, comma-separated set of compression methods.
disabled_filesystems	(empty)	Disable specific file systems, thereby preventing their access, e.g. LocalFileSystem.
disabled_log_types	(empty)	Sets the list of disabled log types.
disabled_optimizers	(empty)	Disable a specific, comma-separated set of optimizers.
duckdb_api	cpp	Specifies which client API/binding opened the database connection, e.g. cpp, capi, cli. The value gets folded into the HTTP User-Agent string DuckDB sends on any HTTP request.
dynamic_or_filter_threshold	50	The maximum amount of OR filters that are generated dynamically from a hash join.
enable_curl_server_cert_verification	on	Enable server side certificate verification for CURL backend.
enable_external_access	on	Allow the database to access external state, e.g. through loading/installing modules, COPY TO/FROM, CSV readers, pandas replacement scans, etc.
enable_external_file_cache	on	Allow the database to cache external files like Parquet in memory.
enable_fsst_vectors	off	Allow scans on FSST compressed segments to emit compressed vectors to utilize late decompression.
enable_geoparquet_conversion	on	Attempt to decode/encode geometry data in/as GeoParquet files if the spatial extension is present.
enable_global_s3_configuration	on	Automatically fetch AWS credentials from environment variables.
enable_http_metadata_cache	off	Whether or not the global http metadata is used to cache HTTP metadata.
enable_logging	1	Enables the logger.
enable_macro_dependencies	on	Enables created MACROs to create dependencies on the referenced objects, such as tables.
enable_optimistic_write	on	Whether or not to optimistically write large appends to disk before committing. Disable this to keep bulk appends in memory, e.g. for in-memory benchmarks.
enable_optimizer	on	Whether the query optimizer is enabled.
enable_profiling	NULL	Enables profiling and sets the output format, which can be JSON, QUERY_TREE, or QUERY_TREE_OPTIMIZER.
enable_progress_bar	on	Enables the progress bar, which prints progress to the terminal during long queries.
enable_progress_bar_print	off	Controls the printing of the progress bar and requires 'enable_progress_bar' to be true.
enable_server_cert_verification	off	Enable server side certificate verification.
enable_view_dependencies	on	Enable created VIEWs to create dependencies on the referenced objects, such as tables.
enabled_log_types	(empty)	Sets the list of enabled log types.
error_on_division_by_zero	on	Throw an error instead of returning NULL when dividing by zero.
errors_as_json	off	Output error messages as structured JSON instead of as a raw string.
experimental_metadata_reuse	on	EXPERIMENTAL: Re-use row group and table metadata when checkpointing.
explain_output	PHYSICAL_ONLY	Configure the output of EXPLAIN statements (ALL, OPTIMIZED_ONLY, PHYSICAL_ONLY).
explain_output_format	PG	Column shape of EXPLAIN output (DUCKDB_NATIVE = native two-column key/value, PG = single QUERY PLAN column with one row per line)
extension_directories	[]	Set the directories to store extensions in.
extension_repository_directory	(empty)	Set the directory in which trusted extension repositories are stored. This is the trust anchor for user-provided repositories, so while signature checking is enabled (allow_unsigned_extensions=false) it can only be set at startup, not while the database is running.
external_file_cache_local_max_block_size	16384	Maximum size in bytes of an external file cache block for local (non-remote) files. Larger reads are split into blocks of this size, which are fetched in parallel.
external_file_cache_remote_max_block_size	2097152	Maximum size in bytes of an external file cache block for remote files (e.g. HTTP/S3). Larger reads are split into blocks of this size, which are fetched in parallel.
external_file_cache_remote_min_block_size	4096	Reads of remote files are rounded out to aligned blocks of this size, so tiny reads do not each cost a request.
external_file_cache_spill	off	Whether evicted external file cache blocks of remote files spill to the temporary directory instead of being dropped, so that they are re-read from there rather than re-fetched from the source.
external_threads	0	The number of external threads that work on DuckDB tasks.
extra_float_digits	1	Sets the number of digits displayed for floating-point values.
extra_http_headers	{}	Extra HTTP headers added to every request
file_search_path	(empty)	A comma separated list of directories to search for input files.
force_column_metadata_reuse	off	Force re-use of row group metadata on a column-level when checkpointing on older storage versions 6 and 7. This breaks storage backward-compatibility with older DuckDB versions.
force_compression	auto	Forces the usage of a specific compression method.
force_dict_fsst_mode	DEFAULT	DEBUG SETTING: pins the dict_fsst string compression mode (case-insensitive). 'DEFAULT' follows storage ownership (serenedb-owned -> auto across all modes; native duckdb -> native modes only); 'AUTO' forces auto across all modes; 'AUTO_NATIVE' forces auto across the native modes only (DICTIONARY, DICT_FSST, FSST_ONLY); or pin one mode: 'DICTIONARY', 'DICT_FSST', 'FSST_ONLY', 'DICT_FSST_PLUS', 'FSST_PLUS'
force_download	off	Forces upfront download of file
force_download_threshold	0	Forces upfront download of files smaller than the given size in bytes
fsync_mode	STANDARD	How to synchronize database file changes to stable storage (STANDARD, NONE or FULL). NONE may cause database corruption after an operating system or hardware crash. FULL uses fullfsync on macOS.
gcs_user_project	NULL	GCS billing project for Requester Pays
geometry_always_xy	NULL	ignore the defined axis order of coordinate reference systems and always treat them as (easting, northing) instead of e.g. (latitude, longitude)
geometry_minimum_shredding_size	30000	Minimum size of a row group to enable GEOMETRY shredding. Set to -1 to disable shredding entirely. Defaults to 1/4th of a row group.
hba	(empty)	Host-based authentication ruleset (pg_hba.conf syntax) as a single string: one rule per line, first match wins, applied to connections opened after the SET. An un-removable local + loopback trust rule is force-prepended so a bad ruleset cannot lock you out; an empty value restores the default (unix trust + SCRAM for TCP). Server-global.
hf_max_per_page	0	Debug option to limit number of items returned in list requests
home_directory	(empty)	Sets the home directory of the database instance.
http_client_pool_capacity	<slt:ignore>	HTTP client pool capacity derived from CPU and async thread counts unless explicitly set
http_keep_alive	on	Keep alive connections. Setting this to false can help when running into connection failures
http_proxy	(empty)	The HTTP proxy host. Defaults to the HTTP_PROXY environment variable.
http_proxy_password	(empty)	The password for the HTTP proxy.
http_proxy_username	(empty)	The username for the HTTP proxy.
http_retries	3	HTTP retries on I/O error
http_retry_backoff	4	Backoff factor for exponentially increasing retry wait time
http_retry_wait_ms	100	Time between retries
http_timeout	30	HTTP timeout read/write/connection/retry (in seconds)
httpfs_connection_caching	on	Enable connection caching for HTTP requests
httpfs_enable_credential_refresh	on	Enable credential refresh for HTTPFS S3 secrets
iceberg_default_format_version	2	The Iceberg format version used when creating a new table without an explicit 'format-version' property. Valid values are 2 and 3.
iceberg_equality_delete_fast_filter	on	Apply byte-comparable equality deletes through a shared columnar flat hash filter instead of a bound expression per delete row. Unsupported types retain the upstream expression path.
iceberg_logging_post_body_truncate_limit	10000	Maximum number of characters of a REST catalog POST body to include in Iceberg log messages. Bodies longer than this are truncated with a trailing '... (truncated)' marker. Set to 0 to omit the body.
iceberg_metadata_log_clock_skew_ms	0	Clock-skew allowance in milliseconds when iceberg_use_metadata_log is enabled. Table metadata up to this far after transaction start is considered visible. Set to 0 for strict timestamp comparisons.
iceberg_test_force_token_expiry	off	DEBUG SETTING: force OAuth2 token expiry for testing automatic refresh
iceberg_unsafe_skip_puffin_verification	off	Skip structural Puffin verification for deletion-vector files. This unsafe compatibility option permits reading invalid bare-blob files written by DuckDB Iceberg 1.5.3.
iceberg_use_metadata_log	off	Use metadata-log to select table metadata as of the transaction start for snapshot isolation. Disable to accept the latest table metadata resolved by the transaction instead
iceberg_use_server_side_scan_planning	off	Whether or not to use server-side scanning planning (if available)
ieee_floating_point_ops	on	Use IEEE 754 behavior for supported floating point operations, returning NAN/INF instead of errors/NULL.
ignore_unknown_crs	off	Ignore unknown Coordinate Reference Systems (CRS) when creating geometry types or importing geospatial data.
immediate_transaction_mode	off	Whether transactions should be started lazily when needed, or immediately when BEGIN TRANSACTION is called.
in_hot_standby	off	Shows whether hot standby is currently active.
index_scan_max_count	2048	The maximum index scan count sets a threshold for index scans. If fewer than MAX(index_scan_max_count, index_scan_percentage * total_row_count) rows match, we perform an index scan instead of a table scan.
index_scan_percentage	0.001	The index scan percentage sets a threshold for index scans. If fewer than MAX(index_scan_max_count, index_scan_percentage * total_row_count) rows match, we perform an index scan instead of a table scan.
initial_column_segment_size	2048	The initial memory (in bytes) reserved for the first transient column segment. Must be a power of two. Internally, we subtract the block header size (typically 8 bytes) for segments with or exceeding 1024 bytes. Subsequent segments double in size until reaching the block size.
integer_datetimes	on	Shows whether datetimes are integer based.
integer_division	on	Whether or not the / operator defaults to integer division, or to floating point division.
IntervalStyle	postgres	Sets the display format for interval values.
is_superuser	on	Shows whether the current session's user is a superuser.
json_geometry_format	wkt	How GEOMETRY values are written to JSON: 'wkt' for Well-Known Text, or 'geojson' for GeoJSON geometry objects. COPY ... TO ... (FORMAT GEOJSON) always writes GeoJSON regardless of this setting.
late_materialization_max_rows	50	The maximum amount of rows in the LIMIT/SAMPLE operator for which we trigger late materialization.
legacy_disable_null_type	off	When enabled, prevent the NULL type from leaving the binder. This was the default behavior prior to DuckDB v2.0.
lock_configuration	off	Whether configurations can be altered.
log_query_path	(empty)	Specifies the path to which queries should be logged. The default is NULL, meaning queries are not logged.
logging_level	<slt:ignore>	Determines which 'severity' of log messages will be logged.
logging_mode	<slt:ignore>	Determines which types of log messages are logged.
logging_storage	<slt:ignore>	Set the logging storage, options are 'memory', 'stdout', 'file', '<custom>'.
match_recognize_max_states	1000000	The maximum number of pattern states MATCH_RECOGNIZE explores for a single match, before it refuses the pattern (0 = no limit). A match is never refused below what matching the pattern without backtracking would take.
max_execution_time	0	The maximum execution time per query in milliseconds (0 = no limit).
max_expression_depth	1000	The maximum expression depth limit in the parser. WARNING: increasing this setting and using very deep expressions might lead to stack overflow errors.
max_memory	<slt:ignore>	The maximum memory of the system (e.g. 1GB).
max_streaming_buffer_size	10.0 MiB	The maximum number of bytes a streaming query result buffers (e.g. 1GB). Queued output stays under this cap, and each engine thread may hold, beyond the queue, the units it is still building or handing over from its current chunk.
max_temp_directory_size	90% of available disk space	The maximum amount of data stored inside the 'temp_directory' (when set) (e.g. 1GB).
max_vacuum_tasks	100	The maximum number of vacuum tasks to schedule during a checkpoint.
memory_limit	<slt:ignore>	The maximum memory of the system (e.g. 1GB).
merge_http_secret_into_s3_request	on	Merges HTTP secret parameters into S3 requests
merge_join_threshold	1000	The maximum number of rows on either table to choose a merge join.
nested_loop_join_threshold	5	The maximum number of rows on either table to choose a nested loop join.
null_order	NULLS_LAST	The NULL ordering used when none is specified (NULLS_FIRST or NULLS_LAST).
operator_memory_limit	NULL	The maximum memory available for query intermediates (sorts, hash tables) per connection (e.g. 256MB).
order_by_non_integer_literal	off	Allow ordering by non-integer literals. Ordering by such literals has no effect. Enabling this relaxes the check to a silent no-op instead of a binder error.
ordered_aggregate_threshold	262144	The number of rows to accumulate before sorting.
parquet_metadata_cache	off	Cache Parquet metadata - useful when reading the same files multiple times
parquet_prefetch_column_gap	NULL	Byte gap under which Parquet prefetch I/O ranges are coalesced (NULL lets the cost model adapt it)
partitioned_write_flush_threshold	524288	The number of rows threshold after which a thread state is flushed when writing using PARTITION_BY.
partitioned_write_max_open_files	100	The maximum amount of files the system can keep open before flushing to disk when writing using PARTITION_BY.
perfect_ht_threshold	12	Threshold in bytes for when to use a perfect hash table.
pg_array_as_varchar	off	Read Postgres arrays as varchar - enables reading mixed dimensional arrays
pg_connection_cache	on	Whether or not to use the connection pooling. This option is deprecated, instead to disable the connection pooling use "SET pg_pool_max_connections=0" for newly attached Postgres databases and "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_connections=0)" for already attached Postgres databases.
pg_connection_limit	<slt:ignore>	The maximum amount of concurrent Postgres connections. This option is deprecated, instead use "SET pg_pool_max_connections = 42" for newly attached Postgres databases and "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_connections=42)" for already attached Postgres databases.
pg_debug_show_queries	off	DEBUG SETTING: print all queries sent to Postgres to stdout
pg_experimental_filter_pushdown	on	Whether or not to use filter pushdown
pg_idle_in_transaction_timeout_millis	NULL	Postgres idle in transaction timeout in milliseconds to set on scan connections
pg_null_byte_replacement	NULL	When writing NULL bytes to Postgres, replace them with the given character
pg_numeric_as_varchar	off	Read Postgres numerics without precision and scale or precision > 38 as varchar instead of double
pg_numeric_nan_as_null	on	Read Postgres numeric NaN value as NULL instead of throwing an error
pg_oauth_token	NULL	OAuth bearer token for PostgreSQL OAUTHBEARER authentication. Takes priority over the PGOAUTHTOKEN environment variable
pg_order_pushdown	on	Push ORDER BY and LIMIT clauses to Postgres (default: true)
pg_pages_per_task	1000	The amount of pages per task
pg_pool_acquire_mode	force	How to acquire connections from the pool: 'force' (always connect, ignore pool limit), 'wait' (block until available), 'try' (fail immediately if unavailable) (default: force)
pg_pool_enable_reaper_thread	on	Whether to enable the connection pool reaper thread, that periodically scans the pool to check the 'max_lifetime_millis' and 'idle_timeout_millis' and closes the connection which exceed the specified values. Either 'max_lifetime_millis' or 'idle_timeout_millis' must be set to a non-zero value for this option to be effective. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', enable_reaper_thread=TRUE)"
pg_pool_enable_thread_local_cache	off	Whether to enable the connection caching in thread-local cache. Such connections are getting pinned to the threads and are not made available to other threads, while still taking the place in the pool. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', enable_thread_local_cache=FALSE)"
pg_pool_health_check_query	SELECT 1	The query that is used to check that the connection is healthy. Setting this option to an empty string disables the health check. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', health_check_query=SELECT 42)"
pg_pool_idle_timeout_millis	60000	Maximum number of milliseconds the connection can be kept idle in the pool. This number is checked when the connection is taken from the pool. When the connection pool reaper thread is enabled ('pg_pool_enable_reaper_thread' option), then this number is checked in background periodically. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', idle_timeout_millis=300000)"
pg_pool_max_connections	<slt:ignore>	Maximum number of connections that are allowed to be cached in a connection pool for each attached Postgres database. This number can be temporary exceeded when parallel scans are used. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_connections=42)"
pg_pool_max_lifetime_millis	0	Maximum number of milliseconds the connection can be kept open. This number is checked when the connection is taken from the pool and returned to the pool. When the connection pool reaper thread is enabled ('pg_pool_enable_reaper_thread' option), then this number is checked in background periodically. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_lifetime_millis=600000)"
pg_pool_wait_timeout_millis	30000	Maximum number of milliseconds to wait when acquiring a connection from a pool where all available connections are already taken. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', wait_timeout_millis=60000)"
pg_staleness_query	NULL	Custom query used in place of the default table staleness query when pg_staleness_query_enabled resolves to true. Must contain a ${SCHEMA} placeholder and return at least 3 columns (identity, name, revision marker). Empty (default) uses the built-in pg_class/xmin query.
pg_staleness_query_enabled	off	Whether or not the table catalog cache checks Postgres for external DDL changes before serving a cache hit. Defaults to the opposite of pg_use_information_schema_introspection when not explicitly set (off for pg protocol compatible databases that may not support the underlying query, on for Postgres).
pg_statement_timeout_millis	NULL	Postgres statement timeout in milliseconds to set on scan connections
pg_use_binary_copy	on	Whether or not to use BINARY copy to read data
pg_use_ctid_scan	on	Whether or not to parallelize scanning using table ctids
pg_use_information_schema_introspection	off	Use SQL-standard information_schema views for ATTACH-time schema discovery instead of pg_catalog.For compatibility with pg protocol compatible databases like spanner, cockroach, redshift, ...
pg_use_text_protocol	off	Whether or not to use TEXT protocol to read data. This is slower, but provides better compatibility with non-Postgres systems
pin_threads	auto	Whether to pin threads to cores. Linux only, and the default is AUTO. AUTO means the setting is on when there are more than 64 cores.
pivot_filter_threshold	20	The threshold determining when a dedicated pivot operator switches from using filtered aggregates to LIST.
pivot_limit	100000	The maximum number of pivot columns in a pivot statement.
prefer_range_joins	off	Force the use of range joins with mixed predicates.
preserve_identifier_case	lowercase	How to fold non-quoted identifiers. 'preserve_case' keeps the case as written, 'lowercase' lowercases them, 'uppercase' uppercases them.
preserve_insertion_order	on	Whether or not to preserve insertion order. If set to false, then the system is allowed to re-order any results that do not contain ORDER BY clauses.
profile_output	(empty)	The file to which profiler output is written. When empty, the output is printed to the terminal.
profiling_coverage	SELECT	The profiling coverage, either SELECT (only SELECT queries) or ALL (all queries are profiled).
profiling_output	(empty)	The file to which profiler output is written. When empty, the output is printed to the terminal.
profiling_renderer_settings	{}	A map of settings passed to the renderer of the profiler output, e.g. {'max_extra_lines': 100}. Settings not recognized by the active renderer are ignored.
progress_bar_time	2000	Configures how long (in milliseconds) a query needs to take before we start printing a progress bar.
read_ahead_depth	-1	The number of scan jobs prefetched ahead of decoding. -1 = automatic, with the backlog being bound by a memory budget, 0 = disabled.
recovery_replay_depth	0	Maximum WAL chunks in flight per inverted index during recovery replay (the prefetch window; bounds replay memory). 0 = auto (4 x cpu threads).
refresh_interval	1000	Background refresh interval (ms) for newly created inverted indexes and search tables. WITH (refresh_interval = ...) overrides it per index or table, ALTER INDEX / ALTER TABLE ... SET changes it later. 0 disables the refresh task. Default: 1000.
regex_match_operator_semantics	partial	Configures whether regex match operators use partial or full string matching.
reindex_interval	0	Periodic reindex interval (ms) for newly created VIEW-backed inverted indexes: a non-zero value creates a job named after the index that runs the ordinary REINDEX road (up_to_date / delta / rebuild) as the index owner, AFTER the interval. Per-index WITH (reindex_interval = ...) overrides; ALTER INDEX SET retunes, creates or drops the job. 0 disables it. Hint-less iceberg sources refresh from the background only when the GLOBAL unsafe_enable_version_guessing is set. Default: 0.
role	none	Sets the current role.
row_group_size	122880	Default columnstore row-group size for newly created inverted indexes. Per-index WITH (row_group_size = ...) overrides it. Reads from existing indexes are unaffected. Default: 122'880.
rtree_index_scan_min_rows	8192	always allow an R-tree index scan when the estimated number of matching rows is at or below this count, regardless of rtree_index_scan_ratio
rtree_index_scan_ratio	0.075	the maximum estimated fraction of a table's rows that a bounding-box filter may match for an R-tree index scan to be used instead of a full table scan
s3_access_key_id	NULL	S3 Access Key ID
s3_allow_recursive_globbing	on	Whether globs on S3-like storage are optimized with recursive strategy (alternative is listing)
s3_endpoint	NULL	S3 Endpoint
s3_kms_key_id	NULL	S3 KMS Key ID
s3_list_concurrency	256	Maximum number of concurrent LIST requests issued while expanding an S3 glob. The window is also bounded by async_threads + 1 and shrinks automatically when the server throttles.
s3_region	NULL	S3 Region
s3_requester_pays	off	S3 use requester pays mode
s3_secret_access_key	NULL	S3 Access Key
s3_session_token	NULL	S3 Session Token
s3_uploader_max_filesize	80GB	Maximum size of an S3 upload
s3_uploader_max_parts_per_file	10000	Maximum number of parts in an S3 multipart upload
s3_url_compatibility_mode	off	Disable Globs and Query Parameters on S3 URLs
s3_url_scheme_aliases	[]	Additional URL schemes routed to the S3-compatible filesystem (e.g. ['oss', 'cos']). Can only be set globally; secrets for aliased schemes need an explicit SCOPE.
s3_url_style	vhost	S3 URL style
s3_use_ssl	on	S3 use SSL
s3_version_id_pinning	off	Pin S3 reads to a specific object version for consistency
scalar_subquery_error_on_multiple_rows	on	Deprecated setting. Throw an error when a scalar subquery returns more than one row. This will become the default behavior. When disabled, an arbitrary row is returned instead.
scheduler_process_partial	on	Partially process tasks before rescheduling. Enabling this allows for more scheduler fairness between separate queries.
schema	public	Sets the default search schema. Equivalent to setting search_path to a single value.
scram_iterations	4096	Sets the iteration count for SCRAM secret generation.
sdb_ai_allow_insecure_endpoint	off	When false, AI functions refuse a secret whose base_url sends requests over plain http:// to a host other than localhost, 127.0.0.0/8 or ::1, because the prompts and the API key would travel unencrypted. Default: false.
sdb_ai_embedding_default_secret	(empty)	Name of the openai secret used by ai_embed and ai_similarity when the call does not pass secret_name. Default: '' (no default).
sdb_ai_embedding_max_batch_size	100	Maximum number of texts ai_embed and ai_similarity send in one embeddings request. Default: 100.
sdb_ai_max_api_calls_per_query	0	Maximum number of AI provider requests a single query may send. 0 = unlimited. Default: 0.
sdb_ai_max_concurrent_requests	16	Maximum number of AI provider requests a query has in flight, across all of its AI calls and threads. Requests run on DuckDB's async I/O threads (async_threads) and on the threads that evaluate the calls. Default: 16.
sdb_ai_max_output_tokens_per_query	0	Maximum number of output tokens, as reported by the provider, a single query may consume; checked before each request, so requests already in flight may exceed it. 0 = unlimited. Default: 0.
sdb_ai_max_retries	3	How many times an AI provider request is retried after a connection error or HTTP 408, 429, 5xx or 529. Default: 3.
sdb_ai_request_timeout	120	Timeout of a single AI provider request, in seconds. Default: 120.
sdb_ai_retry_initial_delay_ms	500	Delay before the first AI provider retry, in milliseconds; each further retry doubles it, up to 60 seconds. A Retry-After response header overrides it, up to 60 seconds. Default: 500.
sdb_ai_system_one_default_secret	(empty)	Name of the typesafe secret used by ai_system_one when the call does not pass secret_name. Default: '' (no default).
sdb_ai_text_default_secret	(empty)	Name of the openai secret used by ai_generate, ai_classify, ai_classify_labels, ai_extract, ai_filter, ai_translate, ai_redact, ai_score, ai_rerank, ai_agg and ai_summarize_agg when the call does not pass secret_name. Default: '' (no default).
sdb_ai_throw_on_error	on	When true, a row whose AI function request fails fails the query; when false, that row returns NULL. Authentication, not-found, validation (422) and exhausted-quota (429 insufficient_quota) errors always fail the query. Default: true.
sdb_ai_throw_on_quota_exceeded	on	When true, exceeding sdb_ai_max_api_calls_per_query or sdb_ai_max_output_tokens_per_query fails the query; when false, the remaining rows return NULL. Default: true.
sdb_compact_target_segments	1	How many segments VACUUM (COMPACT_*) leaves in a search table. 0 or 1 (default) merges every segment into one; a larger N splits the segments into N disjoint groups, merges each group into one segment and stops there, so no single merge holds the whole table. A table with N segments or fewer is left as it is. Default 1.
sdb_disable_top_k_optimization	off	When true, the optimizer skips pulling `ORDER BY <scorer>(...) DESC LIMIT k` into the inverted-index scan, so block-max score pruning never engages. Default: false (optimization on).
sdb_hnsw_ef_search	64	Search-time beam width (ef) for HNSW vector indexes. Higher values improve recall at the cost of latency. The beam is also the result ceiling: a value below the query's LIMIT returns fewer rows than asked for. Default 64.
sdb_ivf_max_search_fanout	16	Maximum number of IVF centroid-tree children expanded per node while descending to the probed clusters. Decouples the descent width from sdb_ivf_search_nprobe: lower values cut centroid work on deep (multi-level) trees at some recall cost. The width applies per node and so compounds over the tree's levels; it is raised when smaller than the width whose compounded value reaches sdb_ivf_search_nprobe, so the descent can always supply the requested number of clusters. Default 16.
sdb_ivf_posting_size	1024	Target IVF posting-list size (leaf cap t), captured into the index config at CREATE INDEX. Smaller values force deeper multi-level centroid trees (useful for testing). Default 1024.
sdb_ivf_sample_factor	0.2	Fraction of rows used to train the IVF centroid tree (sample_size = sample_factor * N), captured into the index config at CREATE INDEX. Any value in (0, 1]. Default 0.2.
sdb_ivf_search_nprobe	8	Number of IVF cluster lists scanned per vector-similarity query. Higher values improve recall at the cost of latency. Default 8.
sdb_job_history_size	1024	Number of recent job runs, across all jobs, that duckdb_job_runs() returns; the oldest run is dropped first. 0 keeps none. Default 1024. Server-global.
sdb_job_max_depth	16	Maximum number of job runs in one chain of EXECUTE JOB calls, where a job's body executes another job; a run that would go deeper fails. Default 16. Server-global.
sdb_levenshtein_max_terms	50	The maximum number of dictionary terms a fuzzy predicate (`ts_levenshtein`) expands to per index segment. Terms closest to the query survive; the rest neither match nor contribute to scoring. Higher values improve recall on wide expansions at the cost of per-query work. 0 removes the cap, so every term within the edit distance matches. Default 50.
sdb_pattern_cache_size	0	Bytes of compiled search patterns (`ts_regexp`, `ts_like`, LIKE and fused alternations over an inverted index) kept across queries, so a pattern is compiled once per server rather than once per query. The least recently used patterns are dropped first; a pattern in use by a running query stays alive until it finishes. 0, the default, keeps nothing: each query compiles its own patterns. Server-global.
sdb_rerank_factor	4	Multiplier applied to LIMIT k to size the candidate pool re-scored with exact distances for a quantized IVF vector-similarity query (pool = ceil(sdb_rerank_factor * k)). Higher values improve recall at the cost of latency; 0 disables reranking (top-k picked by the approximate quantized distance). Fractional values are allowed, but a nonzero factor below 1 is rejected because the pool must cover k. Default 4. Unquantized (quant = 'none') indexes never rerank, regardless of this setting.
sdb_scan_no_split_row_groups	1	A segment with at most this many row groups is always one unit of an inverted-index scan and is never split across workers. Default 1.
sdb_scan_order	auto	The order an inverted-index scan claims its segments in: 'smallest_first' and 'largest_first' order them by live document count; 'order' is best-first by the ORDER BY column's row-group statistics when the query has a scan order (and 'largest_first' otherwise); 'auto' (default) is 'order' under a scan order and 'largest_first' otherwise.
sdb_scan_split	auto	How an inverted-index scan shares a segment between workers: 'tail' gives each worker its own segment and lets an idle worker join the segment with the most row groups left only once no segment is unclaimed; 'always' puts every worker on the same segment until it is claimed; 'never' scans each segment whole on one worker; 'auto' (default) is 'always' under an ORDER BY scan order and 'tail' otherwise.
search_backfill_group_bytes	1073741824	Bytes of existing segments a search-table CREATE INDEX rewrites before swapping them in and moving on. Bounds the build's peak disk (~2x one group) and the length of each publish; a value above the table's size means a single swap. 0 = no limit (one swap for the whole table). Default 1073741824 (1GB).
search_path	<slt:ignore>	Sets the default catalog search path as a comma-separated list of values.
secret_directory	<slt:ignore>	Set the directory in which persistent secrets are stored.
segment_docs_max	0	Document count at which an inverted-index segment writer rolls over to a new on-disk segment. Per-index WITH (segment_docs_max = ...) overrides. 0 = unlimited (memory limit governs).
segment_memory_max	268435456	In-memory bytes an inverted-index or search-table segment writer fills before rolling over to a new on-disk segment (also the CREATE INDEX backfill commit cadence, and half of it is the write buffer a serial search-table statement fills before it starts feeding the index as it goes). Per-object WITH (segment_memory_max = ...) overrides. Default 268435456 (256MB).
server_encoding	UTF8	Shows the server (database) character set encoding.
server_version	18.3	Shows the server version.
server_version_num	180003	Shows the server version as an integer.
session_authorization	postgres	Sets the current session's user name.
show_behavior	SETTING	Configures how SHOW resolves a bare identifier. 'auto' describes a table if one exists, else it describes a setting (deprecated). 'table' always describes a table, and 'setting' always describes a setting.
standard_conforming_strings	on	Causes '...' strings to treat backslashes literally.
standard_vector_size	2048	The compiled-in STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE (read-only).
statement_timeout	0	Aborts any statement that takes more than the specified amount of time (milliseconds without a unit). 0 disables the timeout.
storage_block_prefetch	REMOTE_ONLY	Configures the scenario in which to use storage block prefetching.
storage_compatibility_version	latest	Sets the DuckDB version for which data is serialized to the DuckDB file during checkpointing. Can differ from the version of the DuckDB instance.
streaming_buffer_size	10.0 MiB	The maximum number of bytes a streaming query result buffers (e.g. 1GB). Queued output stays under this cap, and each engine thread may hold, beyond the queue, the units it is still building or handing over from its current chunk.
table_function_identifier_conversion	DISABLE_IMPLICIT_STRING	Configures the use of deprecated implicit conversion of unbound identifiers to strings in table function arguments.
temp_directory	<slt:ignore>	Set the directory to which temporary files are written.
temp_file_encryption	off	Encrypt all temporary files, if the database is encrypted.
threads	<slt:ignore>	The number of total background threads used by the system; a session or transaction value caps the threads its queries use.
TimeZone	Etc/UTC	Sets the time zone for displaying and interpreting time stamps.
tracked_metrics	[*]	A list of metric glob patterns to enable for collection, e.g. ['query.*', 'optimizer.*'].
transaction_isolation	repeatable read	Sets the current transaction's isolation level.
unsafe_disable_etag_checks	off	Disable checks on ETag consistency
unsafe_enable_version_guessing	off	Enable globbing the filesystem (if possible) to find the latest version metadata. This could result in reading an uncommitted version.
validate_external_file_cache	VALIDATE_ALL	The cache validation mode. VALIDATE_ALL is the default, it validates all cache entries., VALIDATE_REMOTE only validates remote cache entries. NO_VALIDATION disables cache validation.
variant_minimum_shredding_size	30000	Minimum size of a row group to have VARIANT shredding enabled. Set to -1 to disable shredding entirely. Defaults to 1/4th of the row group size.
wal_autocheckpoint	16.0 MiB	The WAL size threshold at which to automatically trigger a checkpoint, e.g. 1GB.
wal_autocheckpoint_entries	0	Trigger automatic checkpoint when WAL entry count reaches or exceeds N (0 = disabled).
warnings_as_errors	off	Escalate all warnings to errors.
worker_threads	<slt:ignore>	The number of total background threads used by the system; a session or transaction value caps the threads its queries use.
write_buffer_row_group_count	5	The amount of row groups to buffer in bulk ingestion prior to flushing them together. Reducing this setting can reduce memory consumption.
write_buffer_row_group_memory_limit	<slt:ignore>	The maximum data to buffer in row groups (in bytes) to buffer prior to flushing them together. When either this limit is reached, or write_buffer_row_group_count is reached, we flush the data to disk. Defaults to 20% of the memory limit divided by the thread count.
zstd_min_string_length	4096	The (average) minimum length at which to enable ZSTD compression, defaults to 4096.


# Check that SHOW ALL see updated settings

statement ok
set default_transaction_isolation = 'read committed';


query
SHOW ALL;
----
name	setting	description
__iceberg_unsafe_struct_null_default_interp	NULL	DANGEROUS TESTING-ONLY SETTING: interpret a null Iceberg STRUCT default as an empty struct whose fields use their own defaults. The only non-null value accepted is '{}'.
access_mode	automatic	Access mode of the database (AUTOMATIC, READ_ONLY or READ_WRITE).
allocator_background_threads	off	Whether to enable the allocator background threads.
allocator_bulk_deallocation_flush_threshold	512.0 MiB	If a bulk deallocation larger than this occurs, flush outstanding allocations.
allocator_flush_threshold	134217728B	Peak allocation threshold at which to flush the allocator after completing a task.
allow_asterisks_in_http_paths	off	Allow '*' character in URLs users can query
allow_community_extensions	on	Allow loading extensions build by the community.
allow_extension_repositories	undecided	Whether custom trusted extension repositories are 'allowed', 'forbidden' (which also distrusts existing repositories) or 'undecided' (the default: blocks adding new repositories, but keeps trusting existing ones). While the database is running the setting can only move from 'undecided' to 'allowed' or 'forbidden', or from 'allowed' to 'forbidden'.
allow_extensions_metadata_mismatch	off	Allow to load extensions with no compatible metadata.
allow_persistent_secrets	on	Allow the creation of persistent secrets that are stored and loaded on restarts.
allow_unredacted_secrets	off	Allow printing unredacted secrets.
allow_unsigned_extensions	off	Allow to load extensions with invalid or missing signatures.
allowed_configs	[]	List of configuration options that are ALWAYS allowed to be changed, even when lock_configuration is true.
allowed_directories	[]	List of directories, and directory prefixes, that are ALWAYS allowed to be queried, even when enable_external_access is false.
allowed_paths	[]	List of files that are ALWAYS allowed to be queried, even when enable_external_access is false.
application_name	(empty)	Sets the application name to be reported in statistics and logs.
approximate_join_order_threshold	12	The minimum number of tables in a join to determine the optimal join order approximately instead of exactly.
arrow_large_buffer_size	off	Whether Arrow buffers for strings, blobs, UUIDs and bits should be exported using large buffers.
arrow_lossless_conversion	off	Whenever a DuckDB type does not have a clear native or canonical extension match in Arrow, export the types with a duckdb.type_name extension name.
arrow_output_list_view	off	Whether the export to the Arrow format should use ListView as the physical layout for LIST columns.
arrow_output_version	1.0	Whether strings should be produced by DuckDB in Utf8View format instead of Utf8.
asof_loop_join_threshold	64	The maximum number of rows we need on the left side of an ASOF join to use a nested loop join.
async_threads	<slt:ignore>	The number of total async threads used by the system for tasks like I/O.
auto_checkpoint_skip_wal_threshold	100000	The estimated WAL write size at which point we will skip writing to the WAL and only checkpoint. Skipping writing to the WAL means concurrent commits are blocked while the checkpoint is happening.
auto_fallback_to_full_download	on	Allows automatically falling back to full file downloads when possible.
autoinstall_extension_repository	(empty)	Overrides the custom endpoint for extension installation on autoloading. Falls back to custom_extension_repository, if not specified.
autoinstall_known_extensions	off	Whether known extensions are allowed to be automatically installed when a query depends on them.
autoload_known_extensions	off	Whether known extensions are allowed to be automatically loaded when a query depends on them.
azure_account_name	NULL	Azure account name, when set, the extension will attempt to automatically detect credentials
azure_context_caching	1	Enable/disable the caching of some context when performing queries. This cache is by default enable, and will for a given connection keep a local context when performing a query. If you suspect that the caching is causing some side effect you can try to disable it by setting this option to false.
azure_credential_chain	NULL	Ordered list of Azure credential providers, in string format separated by ';'. E.g. 'cli;workload_identity;managed_identity;env'
azure_endpoint	blob.core.windows.net	Override the azure endpoint for when the Azure credential providers are used.
azure_http_proxy	NULL	Proxy to use when login & performing request to azure. By default it will use the HTTP_PROXY environment variable if set.
azure_http_stats	0	Include http info from the Azure Storage in the explain analyze statement.
azure_proxy_password	NULL	Http proxy password if needed.
azure_proxy_user_name	NULL	Http proxy user name if needed.
azure_read_buffer_size	8388608	Size of the read buffer.
azure_storage_connection_string	NULL	Azure connection string, used for authenticating and configuring azure requests
azure_write_block_size	8388608	Size in bytes of each block for Blob/DFS writes. 0 restores the default (8 MiB). Max 4000 MiB (Azure per-request limit). Azure hard-limits a blob to 50,000 blocks; increase this to write files larger than 50,000 × azure_write_block_size bytes.
azure_write_staged_blocks_per_commit	0	Number of blocks staged before an intermediate CommitBlockList. 0 (default) disables intermediate commits; the full block list is committed on close. Non-zero values make partial writes visible sooner at the cost of extra commit RPCs. Does not affect the 50,000-block blob limit; increase azure_write_block_size for that.
binary_as_string	off	In Parquet files, interpret binary data as a string.
block_allocator_memory	0 bytes	Physical memory that the block allocator is allowed to use. This memory is allocated once, never freed, and cannot be reduced.
bytea_output	hex	Sets the output format for bytea.
ca_cert_file	(empty)	Path to a custom certificate file for self-signed certificates.
cache_local_files	off	Whether the external file cache also caches local files. Remote files are always cached.
Calendar	gregorian	The current calendar
catalog_error_max_schemas	100	The maximum number of schemas in the catalog that the system will scan to generate the "did you mean..." error message.
ch_binary_as_blob	off	Read ClickHouse String/FixedString columns as BLOB instead of VARCHAR
ch_connection_cache	on	Whether to reuse (pool) ClickHouse connections across statements; setting this to false bypasses the connection pool entirely (dynamic kill switch)
ch_debug_show_queries	off	DEBUG SETTING: print all queries sent to ClickHouse to stdout
ch_experimental_filter_pushdown	on	Whether or not to use filter pushdown
ch_order_pushdown	on	Push ORDER BY and LIMIT clauses to ClickHouse (default: true)
ch_pool_acquire_mode	force	How to acquire connections from the pool: 'force' (always connect, ignore pool limit), 'wait' (block until available), 'try' (fail immediately if unavailable) (default: force)
ch_pool_enable_reaper_thread	on	Whether to run the pool reaper thread that periodically closes connections exceeding 'ch_pool_max_lifetime_millis' or 'ch_pool_idle_timeout_millis'
ch_pool_enable_thread_local_cache	off	Whether to enable the connection caching in thread-local cache. Such connections are pinned to their threads and are not made available to other threads, while still taking a place in the pool
ch_pool_idle_timeout_millis	60000	Maximum number of milliseconds a connection can sit idle in the pool; checked on lease and, with the reaper thread enabled, in the background
ch_pool_max_connections	<slt:ignore>	Maximum number of connections that are allowed to be cached in a connection pool for each attached ClickHouse database
ch_pool_max_lifetime_millis	0	Maximum number of milliseconds a connection can be kept open; checked on lease/return and, with the reaper thread enabled, in the background
ch_pool_wait_timeout_millis	30000	Maximum number of milliseconds to wait when acquiring a connection from a pool where all available connections are already taken
ch_statement_timeout_millis	NULL	Maximum milliseconds a ClickHouse scan/execute query may run (0 = unlimited)
checkpoint_on_detach	DEFAULT	Override checkpoint behavior when detaching a database. ENABLED requests a checkpoint, but the checkpoint does not occur if another connection still references the database. DISABLED never checkpoints, DEFAULT defers to the global checkpoint_on_shutdown setting.
checkpoint_threshold	16.0 MiB	The WAL size threshold at which to automatically trigger a checkpoint, e.g. 1GB.
cleanup_interval_step	1	Number of commit ticks between background unreferenced-file cleanup passes for newly created inverted indexes and search tables. WITH (cleanup_interval_step = ...) overrides it per index or table. 0 disables cleanup. Default: 1.
client_encoding	UTF8	Sets the client's character set encoding.
client_min_messages	notice	Sets the message levels that are sent to the client.
compaction_floor_segment_bytes	2097152	Segments of an inverted index or search table below this size count as equal-sized for compaction candidate selection. WITH (compaction_floor_segment_bytes = ...) overrides it per index or table. Default 2097152 (2MB).
compaction_interval	1000	Background compaction interval (ms) for newly created inverted indexes and search tables. WITH (compaction_interval = ...) overrides it per index or table, ALTER INDEX / ALTER TABLE ... SET changes it later. 0 disables background compaction; VACUUM (COMPACT_*) still merges on demand. Default: 1000.
compaction_max_segments	10	Maximum segments of an inverted index or search table merged by one background compaction. WITH (compaction_max_segments = ...) overrides it per index or table. Default 10.
compaction_max_segments_bytes	5368709120	Byte budget of one background compaction of an inverted index or search table (the tier target size). WITH (compaction_max_segments_bytes = ...) overrides it per index or table. Default 5368709120 (5GB).
copy_csv_header_default	off	Whether COPY ... TO a CSV file writes a header line when HEADER is not specified
current_transaction_invalidation_policy	STANDARD_POLICY	Which types of exceptions invalidate the database for the current transaction.
custom_extension_repository	(empty)	Overrides the custom endpoint for extension installation.
custom_user_agent	(empty)	HTTP request metadata that can be set by callers/wrappers to tag their own traffic when DuckDB makes a request.
DateStyle	ISO, MDY	Sets the display format for date and time values.
debug_checkpoint_scan_sleep_ms	0	DEBUG SETTING: time to sleep after a checkpoint has written a table's row groups, before it installs them
default_block_size	262144	The default block size for new duckdb database files. New means that the file is being created and does not yet exist.
default_collation	(empty)	The collation setting used when none is specified.
default_null_order	NULLS_LAST	The NULL ordering used when none is specified (NULLS_FIRST or NULLS_LAST).
default_order	ASCENDING	The order type used when none is specified (ASC or DESC).
default_secret_storage	local_file	Allows switching the default storage for secrets.
default_transaction_invalidation_policy	ALL_ERRORS_INVALIDATE_TRANSACTION	When to invalidate transactions when errors occur. SYNTACTIC_ERRORS_DO_NOT_INVALIDATE means that parser and binder exceptions do not invalidate. ALL_ERRORS_INVALIDATE_TRANSACTION means all errors invalidate a transaction.
default_transaction_isolation	read committed	Sets the transaction isolation level of each new transaction.
default_transaction_read_only	off	Sets the default read-only status of new transactions.
delim_join_as_cte	on	Rewrite delim joins to materialized CTEs during dependent join flattening.
dialect_compatibility_mode	NONE	Enable SQL dialect compatibility for a certain engine, e.g. `SET dialect_compatibility_mode='spark'`.
disable_database_invalidation	on	Disables invalidating the database instance when encountering a fatal error. Should be used with great care, as DuckDB cannot guarantee correct behavior after a fatal error.
disable_parquet_prefetching	off	Disable the prefetching mechanism in Parquet
disable_timestamptz_casts	off	Disable casting from timestamp to timestamptz.
disabled_compression_methods	(empty)	Disable a specific, comma-separated set of compression methods.
disabled_filesystems	(empty)	Disable specific file systems, thereby preventing their access, e.g. LocalFileSystem.
disabled_log_types	(empty)	Sets the list of disabled log types.
disabled_optimizers	(empty)	Disable a specific, comma-separated set of optimizers.
duckdb_api	cpp	Specifies which client API/binding opened the database connection, e.g. cpp, capi, cli. The value gets folded into the HTTP User-Agent string DuckDB sends on any HTTP request.
dynamic_or_filter_threshold	50	The maximum amount of OR filters that are generated dynamically from a hash join.
enable_curl_server_cert_verification	on	Enable server side certificate verification for CURL backend.
enable_external_access	on	Allow the database to access external state, e.g. through loading/installing modules, COPY TO/FROM, CSV readers, pandas replacement scans, etc.
enable_external_file_cache	on	Allow the database to cache external files like Parquet in memory.
enable_fsst_vectors	off	Allow scans on FSST compressed segments to emit compressed vectors to utilize late decompression.
enable_geoparquet_conversion	on	Attempt to decode/encode geometry data in/as GeoParquet files if the spatial extension is present.
enable_global_s3_configuration	on	Automatically fetch AWS credentials from environment variables.
enable_http_metadata_cache	off	Whether or not the global http metadata is used to cache HTTP metadata.
enable_logging	1	Enables the logger.
enable_macro_dependencies	on	Enables created MACROs to create dependencies on the referenced objects, such as tables.
enable_optimistic_write	on	Whether or not to optimistically write large appends to disk before committing. Disable this to keep bulk appends in memory, e.g. for in-memory benchmarks.
enable_optimizer	on	Whether the query optimizer is enabled.
enable_profiling	NULL	Enables profiling and sets the output format, which can be JSON, QUERY_TREE, or QUERY_TREE_OPTIMIZER.
enable_progress_bar	on	Enables the progress bar, which prints progress to the terminal during long queries.
enable_progress_bar_print	off	Controls the printing of the progress bar and requires 'enable_progress_bar' to be true.
enable_server_cert_verification	off	Enable server side certificate verification.
enable_view_dependencies	on	Enable created VIEWs to create dependencies on the referenced objects, such as tables.
enabled_log_types	(empty)	Sets the list of enabled log types.
error_on_division_by_zero	on	Throw an error instead of returning NULL when dividing by zero.
errors_as_json	off	Output error messages as structured JSON instead of as a raw string.
experimental_metadata_reuse	on	EXPERIMENTAL: Re-use row group and table metadata when checkpointing.
explain_output	PHYSICAL_ONLY	Configure the output of EXPLAIN statements (ALL, OPTIMIZED_ONLY, PHYSICAL_ONLY).
explain_output_format	PG	Column shape of EXPLAIN output (DUCKDB_NATIVE = native two-column key/value, PG = single QUERY PLAN column with one row per line)
extension_directories	[]	Set the directories to store extensions in.
extension_repository_directory	(empty)	Set the directory in which trusted extension repositories are stored. This is the trust anchor for user-provided repositories, so while signature checking is enabled (allow_unsigned_extensions=false) it can only be set at startup, not while the database is running.
external_file_cache_local_max_block_size	16384	Maximum size in bytes of an external file cache block for local (non-remote) files. Larger reads are split into blocks of this size, which are fetched in parallel.
external_file_cache_remote_max_block_size	2097152	Maximum size in bytes of an external file cache block for remote files (e.g. HTTP/S3). Larger reads are split into blocks of this size, which are fetched in parallel.
external_file_cache_remote_min_block_size	4096	Reads of remote files are rounded out to aligned blocks of this size, so tiny reads do not each cost a request.
external_file_cache_spill	off	Whether evicted external file cache blocks of remote files spill to the temporary directory instead of being dropped, so that they are re-read from there rather than re-fetched from the source.
external_threads	0	The number of external threads that work on DuckDB tasks.
extra_float_digits	1	Sets the number of digits displayed for floating-point values.
extra_http_headers	{}	Extra HTTP headers added to every request
file_search_path	(empty)	A comma separated list of directories to search for input files.
force_column_metadata_reuse	off	Force re-use of row group metadata on a column-level when checkpointing on older storage versions 6 and 7. This breaks storage backward-compatibility with older DuckDB versions.
force_compression	auto	Forces the usage of a specific compression method.
force_dict_fsst_mode	DEFAULT	DEBUG SETTING: pins the dict_fsst string compression mode (case-insensitive). 'DEFAULT' follows storage ownership (serenedb-owned -> auto across all modes; native duckdb -> native modes only); 'AUTO' forces auto across all modes; 'AUTO_NATIVE' forces auto across the native modes only (DICTIONARY, DICT_FSST, FSST_ONLY); or pin one mode: 'DICTIONARY', 'DICT_FSST', 'FSST_ONLY', 'DICT_FSST_PLUS', 'FSST_PLUS'
force_download	off	Forces upfront download of file
force_download_threshold	0	Forces upfront download of files smaller than the given size in bytes
fsync_mode	STANDARD	How to synchronize database file changes to stable storage (STANDARD, NONE or FULL). NONE may cause database corruption after an operating system or hardware crash. FULL uses fullfsync on macOS.
gcs_user_project	NULL	GCS billing project for Requester Pays
geometry_always_xy	NULL	ignore the defined axis order of coordinate reference systems and always treat them as (easting, northing) instead of e.g. (latitude, longitude)
geometry_minimum_shredding_size	30000	Minimum size of a row group to enable GEOMETRY shredding. Set to -1 to disable shredding entirely. Defaults to 1/4th of a row group.
hba	(empty)	Host-based authentication ruleset (pg_hba.conf syntax) as a single string: one rule per line, first match wins, applied to connections opened after the SET. An un-removable local + loopback trust rule is force-prepended so a bad ruleset cannot lock you out; an empty value restores the default (unix trust + SCRAM for TCP). Server-global.
hf_max_per_page	0	Debug option to limit number of items returned in list requests
home_directory	(empty)	Sets the home directory of the database instance.
http_client_pool_capacity	<slt:ignore>	HTTP client pool capacity derived from CPU and async thread counts unless explicitly set
http_keep_alive	on	Keep alive connections. Setting this to false can help when running into connection failures
http_proxy	(empty)	The HTTP proxy host. Defaults to the HTTP_PROXY environment variable.
http_proxy_password	(empty)	The password for the HTTP proxy.
http_proxy_username	(empty)	The username for the HTTP proxy.
http_retries	3	HTTP retries on I/O error
http_retry_backoff	4	Backoff factor for exponentially increasing retry wait time
http_retry_wait_ms	100	Time between retries
http_timeout	30	HTTP timeout read/write/connection/retry (in seconds)
httpfs_connection_caching	on	Enable connection caching for HTTP requests
httpfs_enable_credential_refresh	on	Enable credential refresh for HTTPFS S3 secrets
iceberg_default_format_version	2	The Iceberg format version used when creating a new table without an explicit 'format-version' property. Valid values are 2 and 3.
iceberg_equality_delete_fast_filter	on	Apply byte-comparable equality deletes through a shared columnar flat hash filter instead of a bound expression per delete row. Unsupported types retain the upstream expression path.
iceberg_logging_post_body_truncate_limit	10000	Maximum number of characters of a REST catalog POST body to include in Iceberg log messages. Bodies longer than this are truncated with a trailing '... (truncated)' marker. Set to 0 to omit the body.
iceberg_metadata_log_clock_skew_ms	0	Clock-skew allowance in milliseconds when iceberg_use_metadata_log is enabled. Table metadata up to this far after transaction start is considered visible. Set to 0 for strict timestamp comparisons.
iceberg_test_force_token_expiry	off	DEBUG SETTING: force OAuth2 token expiry for testing automatic refresh
iceberg_unsafe_skip_puffin_verification	off	Skip structural Puffin verification for deletion-vector files. This unsafe compatibility option permits reading invalid bare-blob files written by DuckDB Iceberg 1.5.3.
iceberg_use_metadata_log	off	Use metadata-log to select table metadata as of the transaction start for snapshot isolation. Disable to accept the latest table metadata resolved by the transaction instead
iceberg_use_server_side_scan_planning	off	Whether or not to use server-side scanning planning (if available)
ieee_floating_point_ops	on	Use IEEE 754 behavior for supported floating point operations, returning NAN/INF instead of errors/NULL.
ignore_unknown_crs	off	Ignore unknown Coordinate Reference Systems (CRS) when creating geometry types or importing geospatial data.
immediate_transaction_mode	off	Whether transactions should be started lazily when needed, or immediately when BEGIN TRANSACTION is called.
in_hot_standby	off	Shows whether hot standby is currently active.
index_scan_max_count	2048	The maximum index scan count sets a threshold for index scans. If fewer than MAX(index_scan_max_count, index_scan_percentage * total_row_count) rows match, we perform an index scan instead of a table scan.
index_scan_percentage	0.001	The index scan percentage sets a threshold for index scans. If fewer than MAX(index_scan_max_count, index_scan_percentage * total_row_count) rows match, we perform an index scan instead of a table scan.
initial_column_segment_size	2048	The initial memory (in bytes) reserved for the first transient column segment. Must be a power of two. Internally, we subtract the block header size (typically 8 bytes) for segments with or exceeding 1024 bytes. Subsequent segments double in size until reaching the block size.
integer_datetimes	on	Shows whether datetimes are integer based.
integer_division	on	Whether or not the / operator defaults to integer division, or to floating point division.
IntervalStyle	postgres	Sets the display format for interval values.
is_superuser	on	Shows whether the current session's user is a superuser.
json_geometry_format	wkt	How GEOMETRY values are written to JSON: 'wkt' for Well-Known Text, or 'geojson' for GeoJSON geometry objects. COPY ... TO ... (FORMAT GEOJSON) always writes GeoJSON regardless of this setting.
late_materialization_max_rows	50	The maximum amount of rows in the LIMIT/SAMPLE operator for which we trigger late materialization.
legacy_disable_null_type	off	When enabled, prevent the NULL type from leaving the binder. This was the default behavior prior to DuckDB v2.0.
lock_configuration	off	Whether configurations can be altered.
log_query_path	(empty)	Specifies the path to which queries should be logged. The default is NULL, meaning queries are not logged.
logging_level	<slt:ignore>	Determines which 'severity' of log messages will be logged.
logging_mode	<slt:ignore>	Determines which types of log messages are logged.
logging_storage	<slt:ignore>	Set the logging storage, options are 'memory', 'stdout', 'file', '<custom>'.
match_recognize_max_states	1000000	The maximum number of pattern states MATCH_RECOGNIZE explores for a single match, before it refuses the pattern (0 = no limit). A match is never refused below what matching the pattern without backtracking would take.
max_execution_time	0	The maximum execution time per query in milliseconds (0 = no limit).
max_expression_depth	1000	The maximum expression depth limit in the parser. WARNING: increasing this setting and using very deep expressions might lead to stack overflow errors.
max_memory	<slt:ignore>	The maximum memory of the system (e.g. 1GB).
max_streaming_buffer_size	10.0 MiB	The maximum number of bytes a streaming query result buffers (e.g. 1GB). Queued output stays under this cap, and each engine thread may hold, beyond the queue, the units it is still building or handing over from its current chunk.
max_temp_directory_size	90% of available disk space	The maximum amount of data stored inside the 'temp_directory' (when set) (e.g. 1GB).
max_vacuum_tasks	100	The maximum number of vacuum tasks to schedule during a checkpoint.
memory_limit	<slt:ignore>	The maximum memory of the system (e.g. 1GB).
merge_http_secret_into_s3_request	on	Merges HTTP secret parameters into S3 requests
merge_join_threshold	1000	The maximum number of rows on either table to choose a merge join.
nested_loop_join_threshold	5	The maximum number of rows on either table to choose a nested loop join.
null_order	NULLS_LAST	The NULL ordering used when none is specified (NULLS_FIRST or NULLS_LAST).
operator_memory_limit	NULL	The maximum memory available for query intermediates (sorts, hash tables) per connection (e.g. 256MB).
order_by_non_integer_literal	off	Allow ordering by non-integer literals. Ordering by such literals has no effect. Enabling this relaxes the check to a silent no-op instead of a binder error.
ordered_aggregate_threshold	262144	The number of rows to accumulate before sorting.
parquet_metadata_cache	off	Cache Parquet metadata - useful when reading the same files multiple times
parquet_prefetch_column_gap	NULL	Byte gap under which Parquet prefetch I/O ranges are coalesced (NULL lets the cost model adapt it)
partitioned_write_flush_threshold	524288	The number of rows threshold after which a thread state is flushed when writing using PARTITION_BY.
partitioned_write_max_open_files	100	The maximum amount of files the system can keep open before flushing to disk when writing using PARTITION_BY.
perfect_ht_threshold	12	Threshold in bytes for when to use a perfect hash table.
pg_array_as_varchar	off	Read Postgres arrays as varchar - enables reading mixed dimensional arrays
pg_connection_cache	on	Whether or not to use the connection pooling. This option is deprecated, instead to disable the connection pooling use "SET pg_pool_max_connections=0" for newly attached Postgres databases and "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_connections=0)" for already attached Postgres databases.
pg_connection_limit	<slt:ignore>	The maximum amount of concurrent Postgres connections. This option is deprecated, instead use "SET pg_pool_max_connections = 42" for newly attached Postgres databases and "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_connections=42)" for already attached Postgres databases.
pg_debug_show_queries	off	DEBUG SETTING: print all queries sent to Postgres to stdout
pg_experimental_filter_pushdown	on	Whether or not to use filter pushdown
pg_idle_in_transaction_timeout_millis	NULL	Postgres idle in transaction timeout in milliseconds to set on scan connections
pg_null_byte_replacement	NULL	When writing NULL bytes to Postgres, replace them with the given character
pg_numeric_as_varchar	off	Read Postgres numerics without precision and scale or precision > 38 as varchar instead of double
pg_numeric_nan_as_null	on	Read Postgres numeric NaN value as NULL instead of throwing an error
pg_oauth_token	NULL	OAuth bearer token for PostgreSQL OAUTHBEARER authentication. Takes priority over the PGOAUTHTOKEN environment variable
pg_order_pushdown	on	Push ORDER BY and LIMIT clauses to Postgres (default: true)
pg_pages_per_task	1000	The amount of pages per task
pg_pool_acquire_mode	force	How to acquire connections from the pool: 'force' (always connect, ignore pool limit), 'wait' (block until available), 'try' (fail immediately if unavailable) (default: force)
pg_pool_enable_reaper_thread	on	Whether to enable the connection pool reaper thread, that periodically scans the pool to check the 'max_lifetime_millis' and 'idle_timeout_millis' and closes the connection which exceed the specified values. Either 'max_lifetime_millis' or 'idle_timeout_millis' must be set to a non-zero value for this option to be effective. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', enable_reaper_thread=TRUE)"
pg_pool_enable_thread_local_cache	off	Whether to enable the connection caching in thread-local cache. Such connections are getting pinned to the threads and are not made available to other threads, while still taking the place in the pool. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', enable_thread_local_cache=FALSE)"
pg_pool_health_check_query	SELECT 1	The query that is used to check that the connection is healthy. Setting this option to an empty string disables the health check. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', health_check_query=SELECT 42)"
pg_pool_idle_timeout_millis	60000	Maximum number of milliseconds the connection can be kept idle in the pool. This number is checked when the connection is taken from the pool. When the connection pool reaper thread is enabled ('pg_pool_enable_reaper_thread' option), then this number is checked in background periodically. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', idle_timeout_millis=300000)"
pg_pool_max_connections	<slt:ignore>	Maximum number of connections that are allowed to be cached in a connection pool for each attached Postgres database. This number can be temporary exceeded when parallel scans are used. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_connections=42)"
pg_pool_max_lifetime_millis	0	Maximum number of milliseconds the connection can be kept open. This number is checked when the connection is taken from the pool and returned to the pool. When the connection pool reaper thread is enabled ('pg_pool_enable_reaper_thread' option), then this number is checked in background periodically. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', max_lifetime_millis=600000)"
pg_pool_wait_timeout_millis	30000	Maximum number of milliseconds to wait when acquiring a connection from a pool where all available connections are already taken. This option only applies to newly attached Postgres databases, to configure a database that is already attached use "FROM postgres_configure_pool(catalog_name='my_attached_postgres_db', wait_timeout_millis=60000)"
pg_staleness_query	NULL	Custom query used in place of the default table staleness query when pg_staleness_query_enabled resolves to true. Must contain a ${SCHEMA} placeholder and return at least 3 columns (identity, name, revision marker). Empty (default) uses the built-in pg_class/xmin query.
pg_staleness_query_enabled	off	Whether or not the table catalog cache checks Postgres for external DDL changes before serving a cache hit. Defaults to the opposite of pg_use_information_schema_introspection when not explicitly set (off for pg protocol compatible databases that may not support the underlying query, on for Postgres).
pg_statement_timeout_millis	NULL	Postgres statement timeout in milliseconds to set on scan connections
pg_use_binary_copy	on	Whether or not to use BINARY copy to read data
pg_use_ctid_scan	on	Whether or not to parallelize scanning using table ctids
pg_use_information_schema_introspection	off	Use SQL-standard information_schema views for ATTACH-time schema discovery instead of pg_catalog.For compatibility with pg protocol compatible databases like spanner, cockroach, redshift, ...
pg_use_text_protocol	off	Whether or not to use TEXT protocol to read data. This is slower, but provides better compatibility with non-Postgres systems
pin_threads	auto	Whether to pin threads to cores. Linux only, and the default is AUTO. AUTO means the setting is on when there are more than 64 cores.
pivot_filter_threshold	20	The threshold determining when a dedicated pivot operator switches from using filtered aggregates to LIST.
pivot_limit	100000	The maximum number of pivot columns in a pivot statement.
prefer_range_joins	off	Force the use of range joins with mixed predicates.
preserve_identifier_case	lowercase	How to fold non-quoted identifiers. 'preserve_case' keeps the case as written, 'lowercase' lowercases them, 'uppercase' uppercases them.
preserve_insertion_order	on	Whether or not to preserve insertion order. If set to false, then the system is allowed to re-order any results that do not contain ORDER BY clauses.
profile_output	(empty)	The file to which profiler output is written. When empty, the output is printed to the terminal.
profiling_coverage	SELECT	The profiling coverage, either SELECT (only SELECT queries) or ALL (all queries are profiled).
profiling_output	(empty)	The file to which profiler output is written. When empty, the output is printed to the terminal.
profiling_renderer_settings	{}	A map of settings passed to the renderer of the profiler output, e.g. {'max_extra_lines': 100}. Settings not recognized by the active renderer are ignored.
progress_bar_time	2000	Configures how long (in milliseconds) a query needs to take before we start printing a progress bar.
read_ahead_depth	-1	The number of scan jobs prefetched ahead of decoding. -1 = automatic, with the backlog being bound by a memory budget, 0 = disabled.
recovery_replay_depth	0	Maximum WAL chunks in flight per inverted index during recovery replay (the prefetch window; bounds replay memory). 0 = auto (4 x cpu threads).
refresh_interval	1000	Background refresh interval (ms) for newly created inverted indexes and search tables. WITH (refresh_interval = ...) overrides it per index or table, ALTER INDEX / ALTER TABLE ... SET changes it later. 0 disables the refresh task. Default: 1000.
regex_match_operator_semantics	partial	Configures whether regex match operators use partial or full string matching.
reindex_interval	0	Periodic reindex interval (ms) for newly created VIEW-backed inverted indexes: a non-zero value creates a job named after the index that runs the ordinary REINDEX road (up_to_date / delta / rebuild) as the index owner, AFTER the interval. Per-index WITH (reindex_interval = ...) overrides; ALTER INDEX SET retunes, creates or drops the job. 0 disables it. Hint-less iceberg sources refresh from the background only when the GLOBAL unsafe_enable_version_guessing is set. Default: 0.
role	none	Sets the current role.
row_group_size	122880	Default columnstore row-group size for newly created inverted indexes. Per-index WITH (row_group_size = ...) overrides it. Reads from existing indexes are unaffected. Default: 122'880.
rtree_index_scan_min_rows	8192	always allow an R-tree index scan when the estimated number of matching rows is at or below this count, regardless of rtree_index_scan_ratio
rtree_index_scan_ratio	0.075	the maximum estimated fraction of a table's rows that a bounding-box filter may match for an R-tree index scan to be used instead of a full table scan
s3_access_key_id	NULL	S3 Access Key ID
s3_allow_recursive_globbing	on	Whether globs on S3-like storage are optimized with recursive strategy (alternative is listing)
s3_endpoint	NULL	S3 Endpoint
s3_kms_key_id	NULL	S3 KMS Key ID
s3_list_concurrency	256	Maximum number of concurrent LIST requests issued while expanding an S3 glob. The window is also bounded by async_threads + 1 and shrinks automatically when the server throttles.
s3_region	NULL	S3 Region
s3_requester_pays	off	S3 use requester pays mode
s3_secret_access_key	NULL	S3 Access Key
s3_session_token	NULL	S3 Session Token
s3_uploader_max_filesize	80GB	Maximum size of an S3 upload
s3_uploader_max_parts_per_file	10000	Maximum number of parts in an S3 multipart upload
s3_url_compatibility_mode	off	Disable Globs and Query Parameters on S3 URLs
s3_url_scheme_aliases	[]	Additional URL schemes routed to the S3-compatible filesystem (e.g. ['oss', 'cos']). Can only be set globally; secrets for aliased schemes need an explicit SCOPE.
s3_url_style	vhost	S3 URL style
s3_use_ssl	on	S3 use SSL
s3_version_id_pinning	off	Pin S3 reads to a specific object version for consistency
scalar_subquery_error_on_multiple_rows	on	Deprecated setting. Throw an error when a scalar subquery returns more than one row. This will become the default behavior. When disabled, an arbitrary row is returned instead.
scheduler_process_partial	on	Partially process tasks before rescheduling. Enabling this allows for more scheduler fairness between separate queries.
schema	public	Sets the default search schema. Equivalent to setting search_path to a single value.
scram_iterations	4096	Sets the iteration count for SCRAM secret generation.
sdb_ai_allow_insecure_endpoint	off	When false, AI functions refuse a secret whose base_url sends requests over plain http:// to a host other than localhost, 127.0.0.0/8 or ::1, because the prompts and the API key would travel unencrypted. Default: false.
sdb_ai_embedding_default_secret	(empty)	Name of the openai secret used by ai_embed and ai_similarity when the call does not pass secret_name. Default: '' (no default).
sdb_ai_embedding_max_batch_size	100	Maximum number of texts ai_embed and ai_similarity send in one embeddings request. Default: 100.
sdb_ai_max_api_calls_per_query	0	Maximum number of AI provider requests a single query may send. 0 = unlimited. Default: 0.
sdb_ai_max_concurrent_requests	16	Maximum number of AI provider requests a query has in flight, across all of its AI calls and threads. Requests run on DuckDB's async I/O threads (async_threads) and on the threads that evaluate the calls. Default: 16.
sdb_ai_max_output_tokens_per_query	0	Maximum number of output tokens, as reported by the provider, a single query may consume; checked before each request, so requests already in flight may exceed it. 0 = unlimited. Default: 0.
sdb_ai_max_retries	3	How many times an AI provider request is retried after a connection error or HTTP 408, 429, 5xx or 529. Default: 3.
sdb_ai_request_timeout	120	Timeout of a single AI provider request, in seconds. Default: 120.
sdb_ai_retry_initial_delay_ms	500	Delay before the first AI provider retry, in milliseconds; each further retry doubles it, up to 60 seconds. A Retry-After response header overrides it, up to 60 seconds. Default: 500.
sdb_ai_system_one_default_secret	(empty)	Name of the typesafe secret used by ai_system_one when the call does not pass secret_name. Default: '' (no default).
sdb_ai_text_default_secret	(empty)	Name of the openai secret used by ai_generate, ai_classify, ai_classify_labels, ai_extract, ai_filter, ai_translate, ai_redact, ai_score, ai_rerank, ai_agg and ai_summarize_agg when the call does not pass secret_name. Default: '' (no default).
sdb_ai_throw_on_error	on	When true, a row whose AI function request fails fails the query; when false, that row returns NULL. Authentication, not-found, validation (422) and exhausted-quota (429 insufficient_quota) errors always fail the query. Default: true.
sdb_ai_throw_on_quota_exceeded	on	When true, exceeding sdb_ai_max_api_calls_per_query or sdb_ai_max_output_tokens_per_query fails the query; when false, the remaining rows return NULL. Default: true.
sdb_compact_target_segments	1	How many segments VACUUM (COMPACT_*) leaves in a search table. 0 or 1 (default) merges every segment into one; a larger N splits the segments into N disjoint groups, merges each group into one segment and stops there, so no single merge holds the whole table. A table with N segments or fewer is left as it is. Default 1.
sdb_disable_top_k_optimization	off	When true, the optimizer skips pulling `ORDER BY <scorer>(...) DESC LIMIT k` into the inverted-index scan, so block-max score pruning never engages. Default: false (optimization on).
sdb_hnsw_ef_search	64	Search-time beam width (ef) for HNSW vector indexes. Higher values improve recall at the cost of latency. The beam is also the result ceiling: a value below the query's LIMIT returns fewer rows than asked for. Default 64.
sdb_ivf_max_search_fanout	16	Maximum number of IVF centroid-tree children expanded per node while descending to the probed clusters. Decouples the descent width from sdb_ivf_search_nprobe: lower values cut centroid work on deep (multi-level) trees at some recall cost. The width applies per node and so compounds over the tree's levels; it is raised when smaller than the width whose compounded value reaches sdb_ivf_search_nprobe, so the descent can always supply the requested number of clusters. Default 16.
sdb_ivf_posting_size	1024	Target IVF posting-list size (leaf cap t), captured into the index config at CREATE INDEX. Smaller values force deeper multi-level centroid trees (useful for testing). Default 1024.
sdb_ivf_sample_factor	0.2	Fraction of rows used to train the IVF centroid tree (sample_size = sample_factor * N), captured into the index config at CREATE INDEX. Any value in (0, 1]. Default 0.2.
sdb_ivf_search_nprobe	8	Number of IVF cluster lists scanned per vector-similarity query. Higher values improve recall at the cost of latency. Default 8.
sdb_job_history_size	1024	Number of recent job runs, across all jobs, that duckdb_job_runs() returns; the oldest run is dropped first. 0 keeps none. Default 1024. Server-global.
sdb_job_max_depth	16	Maximum number of job runs in one chain of EXECUTE JOB calls, where a job's body executes another job; a run that would go deeper fails. Default 16. Server-global.
sdb_levenshtein_max_terms	50	The maximum number of dictionary terms a fuzzy predicate (`ts_levenshtein`) expands to per index segment. Terms closest to the query survive; the rest neither match nor contribute to scoring. Higher values improve recall on wide expansions at the cost of per-query work. 0 removes the cap, so every term within the edit distance matches. Default 50.
sdb_pattern_cache_size	0	Bytes of compiled search patterns (`ts_regexp`, `ts_like`, LIKE and fused alternations over an inverted index) kept across queries, so a pattern is compiled once per server rather than once per query. The least recently used patterns are dropped first; a pattern in use by a running query stays alive until it finishes. 0, the default, keeps nothing: each query compiles its own patterns. Server-global.
sdb_rerank_factor	4	Multiplier applied to LIMIT k to size the candidate pool re-scored with exact distances for a quantized IVF vector-similarity query (pool = ceil(sdb_rerank_factor * k)). Higher values improve recall at the cost of latency; 0 disables reranking (top-k picked by the approximate quantized distance). Fractional values are allowed, but a nonzero factor below 1 is rejected because the pool must cover k. Default 4. Unquantized (quant = 'none') indexes never rerank, regardless of this setting.
sdb_scan_no_split_row_groups	1	A segment with at most this many row groups is always one unit of an inverted-index scan and is never split across workers. Default 1.
sdb_scan_order	auto	The order an inverted-index scan claims its segments in: 'smallest_first' and 'largest_first' order them by live document count; 'order' is best-first by the ORDER BY column's row-group statistics when the query has a scan order (and 'largest_first' otherwise); 'auto' (default) is 'order' under a scan order and 'largest_first' otherwise.
sdb_scan_split	auto	How an inverted-index scan shares a segment between workers: 'tail' gives each worker its own segment and lets an idle worker join the segment with the most row groups left only once no segment is unclaimed; 'always' puts every worker on the same segment until it is claimed; 'never' scans each segment whole on one worker; 'auto' (default) is 'always' under an ORDER BY scan order and 'tail' otherwise.
search_backfill_group_bytes	1073741824	Bytes of existing segments a search-table CREATE INDEX rewrites before swapping them in and moving on. Bounds the build's peak disk (~2x one group) and the length of each publish; a value above the table's size means a single swap. 0 = no limit (one swap for the whole table). Default 1073741824 (1GB).
search_path	<slt:ignore>	Sets the default catalog search path as a comma-separated list of values.
secret_directory	<slt:ignore>	Set the directory in which persistent secrets are stored.
segment_docs_max	0	Document count at which an inverted-index segment writer rolls over to a new on-disk segment. Per-index WITH (segment_docs_max = ...) overrides. 0 = unlimited (memory limit governs).
segment_memory_max	268435456	In-memory bytes an inverted-index or search-table segment writer fills before rolling over to a new on-disk segment (also the CREATE INDEX backfill commit cadence, and half of it is the write buffer a serial search-table statement fills before it starts feeding the index as it goes). Per-object WITH (segment_memory_max = ...) overrides. Default 268435456 (256MB).
server_encoding	UTF8	Shows the server (database) character set encoding.
server_version	18.3	Shows the server version.
server_version_num	180003	Shows the server version as an integer.
session_authorization	postgres	Sets the current session's user name.
show_behavior	SETTING	Configures how SHOW resolves a bare identifier. 'auto' describes a table if one exists, else it describes a setting (deprecated). 'table' always describes a table, and 'setting' always describes a setting.
standard_conforming_strings	on	Causes '...' strings to treat backslashes literally.
standard_vector_size	2048	The compiled-in STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE (read-only).
statement_timeout	0	Aborts any statement that takes more than the specified amount of time (milliseconds without a unit). 0 disables the timeout.
storage_block_prefetch	REMOTE_ONLY	Configures the scenario in which to use storage block prefetching.
storage_compatibility_version	latest	Sets the DuckDB version for which data is serialized to the DuckDB file during checkpointing. Can differ from the version of the DuckDB instance.
streaming_buffer_size	10.0 MiB	The maximum number of bytes a streaming query result buffers (e.g. 1GB). Queued output stays under this cap, and each engine thread may hold, beyond the queue, the units it is still building or handing over from its current chunk.
table_function_identifier_conversion	DISABLE_IMPLICIT_STRING	Configures the use of deprecated implicit conversion of unbound identifiers to strings in table function arguments.
temp_directory	<slt:ignore>	Set the directory to which temporary files are written.
temp_file_encryption	off	Encrypt all temporary files, if the database is encrypted.
threads	<slt:ignore>	The number of total background threads used by the system; a session or transaction value caps the threads its queries use.
TimeZone	Etc/UTC	Sets the time zone for displaying and interpreting time stamps.
tracked_metrics	[*]	A list of metric glob patterns to enable for collection, e.g. ['query.*', 'optimizer.*'].
transaction_isolation	read committed	Sets the current transaction's isolation level.
unsafe_disable_etag_checks	off	Disable checks on ETag consistency
unsafe_enable_version_guessing	off	Enable globbing the filesystem (if possible) to find the latest version metadata. This could result in reading an uncommitted version.
validate_external_file_cache	VALIDATE_ALL	The cache validation mode. VALIDATE_ALL is the default, it validates all cache entries., VALIDATE_REMOTE only validates remote cache entries. NO_VALIDATION disables cache validation.
variant_minimum_shredding_size	30000	Minimum size of a row group to have VARIANT shredding enabled. Set to -1 to disable shredding entirely. Defaults to 1/4th of the row group size.
wal_autocheckpoint	16.0 MiB	The WAL size threshold at which to automatically trigger a checkpoint, e.g. 1GB.
wal_autocheckpoint_entries	0	Trigger automatic checkpoint when WAL entry count reaches or exceeds N (0 = disabled).
warnings_as_errors	off	Escalate all warnings to errors.
worker_threads	<slt:ignore>	The number of total background threads used by the system; a session or transaction value caps the threads its queries use.
write_buffer_row_group_count	5	The amount of row groups to buffer in bulk ingestion prior to flushing them together. Reducing this setting can reduce memory consumption.
write_buffer_row_group_memory_limit	<slt:ignore>	The maximum data to buffer in row groups (in bytes) to buffer prior to flushing them together. When either this limit is reached, or write_buffer_row_group_count is reached, we flush the data to disk. Defaults to 20% of the memory limit divided by the thread count.
zstd_min_string_length	4096	The (average) minimum length at which to enable ZSTD compression, defaults to 4096.
